{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you shall eat and be satisfied</b> etc. From here we say three blessings in birkat ha-mazon. <b>And you shall eat and be satisfied and bless</b> — that one blesses over the eating, this is the blessing of ha-Zan. <b>And you shall bless HaShem your Elohim</b> — to include the head of the household." "<b>Upon the land.</b> This is the blessing of the land — Nodeh lekha HaShem etc." "<b>The good that He has given you.</b> This is the blessing of Boneh Yerushalayim, as it is written: 'this good mountain and the Lebanon.' Now, after eating, when one is satisfied and his soul is sated with food, he needs to bless — all the more so at the outset, when he is hungry and craving and rejoicing over the eating, that he needs to say the blessing of ha-Motzi." "<b>And you shall eat and be satisfied and bless.</b> Here is a hint to the three who require zimun: 'and you shall eat' — one; 'and be satisfied' — two; 'and bless' — third."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:10.799168854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}